---
import { AGENT_STEPS, CSV_STEPS, LINEAR, MCP_MANUAL } from '@lib/compare/linear-alternative';

const PATHS = [
  {
    id: 'la-csv',
    title: 'CSV import',
    when: 'At launch, for any amount of history',
    steps: CSV_STEPS,
    link: { href: LINEAR.exporting.href, label: LINEAR.exporting.label, external: true },
  },
  {
    id: 'la-agent',
    title: 'An agent connected to both',
    when: 'For the unresolved issues you still need',
    steps: AGENT_STEPS,
    link: { href: MCP_MANUAL, label: 'Connecting an agent', external: false },
  },
];
---

<section id="la-switching" class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="la-switching-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[680px]">
      <h2 id="la-switching-title" class="h2">
        Moving issues over from Linear.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        There is no native Linear importer. Two paths work, and both need a person to check the result: the generic CSV
        importer for bulk history, or an agent that reads Linear and writes to Nothing Left while you review each
        mapping.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 md:mt-14 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
      {PATHS.map(path => (
        <div class="panel" aria-labelledby={`${path.id}-title`} role="group">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <h3 id={`${path.id}-title`} class="h3">
              {path.title}
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-2">{path.when}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="panel-pad">
            <ol class="steps-list">
              {path.steps.map(step => (
                <li class="prose text-base">
                  <strong>{step.title}.</strong> {step.body}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <p class="mt-6 text-sm">
              <a class="link" href={path.link.href} rel={path.link.external ? 'noopener' : undefined}>
                {path.link.label}
                <span class:list={['arr', { ext: path.link.external }]} aria-hidden="true">
                  {path.link.external ? '↗' : '→'}
                </span>
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-[680px] text-sm text-fg-2">
      Neither path carries over everything: plan for attachments, full history, comment authorship and Linear-only
      objects such as initiatives to need a decision. Linear’s MCP server and its CSV exports are described on its own
      pages.{' '}
      <a class="link font-normal" href={LINEAR.mcp.href} rel="noopener">
        {LINEAR.mcp.label}
        <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
